1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
In this video, we're going to show you how you can map the visible attack surface in BurpSuite.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Now before you start, we recommend that you set an initial test scope before you start mapping the application.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
If you'd like more information on this, you can see our documentation page on setting the initial test scope.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Now the first thing we're going to do is open Burp's browser.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,000
To do this, we're going to navigate to the proxy tab, intercept, and then click open browser.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
When the browser has opened, we're going to navigate to our target application.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:46,000
For the purposes of the demo, we're going to go to ginindjuice.shop, which is a purposely vulnerable application which we at Portsberger have made, which is designed for testing vulnerability scanners.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Now, without closing the browser, we're going to go back into Burp, go to target, sitemap, and then you should see a node in the sitemap.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
For the application which we just navigated to.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:04,000
If you don't see that node, you should go to the dashboard and make sure that the live passive crawl from proxy task is enabled.

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
This task will just add items to the sitemap as traffic is proxied through Burp.

12
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Now, if you're using BurpSuite Professional, you can now start an automated crawl of the website.

13
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
To do this, we're going to go back to the sitemap and right click the root node of this site, which is here, and then click scan.

14
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
If there are any logins which you need to be able to crawl the site, you should go to the application login tab and then add the credentials here.

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Once you've done that, you can go back to the scan details tab, make sure that the scan type is selected to be crawl, and then click OK.

16
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:49,000
This one I'll start the scan and the crawl of the application, and you should notice that the sitemap automatically populates itself as the scanner discovers more content.

17
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:58,000
While the scan runs, you can also go back to the browser and explore the website yourself, identify any high risk functionality.

18
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:07,000
If you're using BurpSuite Community Edition, you should make sure that you fully explore the application yourself using Burp's browser.

19
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:15,000
If you have any application login credentials, or you can create your own user, you should log in and explore the authenticated areas of the site as well.

20
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Now, in the sitemap, you should notice that some endpoints are greyed out. These are locations that have been explicitly referenced in a response, but have not yet been requested.

21
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:33,000
If you want to discover additional content based on those endpoints, you can select one which is interesting to you. For example, I'll select this one here.

22
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Right click it, and then go to requesting browser, and then in original session. A dialog will now open with a URL for this request. To open this request, you can just copy the URL, and then paste it into Burp's browser.

23
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:02,000
You can see that you'll be redirected shortly, and then the request has been made. You should continue to populate the sitemap until you have requested all visible locations that are interesting and within your scope.

24
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:07,000
You should continue to populate the sitemap until you have requested the site.

25
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
You should continue to populate the site. You should continue to populate the site. You should continue to populate the site.

26
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
You should continue to populate the site. You should continue to populate the site. You should continue to populate the site. You should continue to populate the site.

